# Contact form — Neon Postgres connection string
#
# You do NOT normally set this by hand. In the Vercel dashboard go to
# Storage → Marketplace → Neon, attach a database to this project, and Vercel
# injects DATABASE_URL into every environment automatically.
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` only if you want to run the API function
# locally with `vercel dev` against the same database. Unlike the old Appwrite
# setup, this value is a real secret: it never reaches the browser, it is only
# read inside api/contact.js on the server. Never prefix it with VITE_ —
# that would publish it in the client bundle.
#
# Grab the value from the Neon console → your project → Connection string.

DATABASE_URL=

# Note: `npm run dev` (plain Vite) serves the site but not /api, so the contact
# form will report a network error locally. Use `vercel dev` to exercise it.
